{%- comment -%}
  Evoloop — homepage is intentionally NOT a marketing page.

  Decision (2026-09-05): the Shopify storefront has no homepage — only product
  detail pages. Marketing lives on the Next.js site, which deep-links straight
  into Shopify PDPs. Shopify still serves the store root URL from the index
  template, so this template immediately redirects '/' to the featured product
  chosen in Theme settings > "Evoloop redirect" > "Redirect homepage to".
  When the setting is blank the store falls back to /collections/all so the
  root never dead-ends.

  To bring back a marketing homepage later: re-create templates/index.json and
  drop in sections such as 'evoloop-hero' / 'marquee' / 'product-list'.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign redirect_target = settings.home_redirect_target
  if redirect_target == blank
    assign redirect_target = '/collections/all'
  endif
-%}
<script>
  window.location.replace({{ redirect_target | json }});
</script>
<noscript>
  <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ redirect_target | escape }}">
</noscript>
<div
  class="evo-home-redirect"
  style="min-height: 60vh; display: grid; place-items: center; padding: 2rem; text-align: center;"
>
  <p style="margin: 0">
    <a href="{{ redirect_target }}">Continue to {{ redirect_target }}</a>
  </p>
</div>
